  "title": "She Swore I Worked There Because Of My Jacket. Security Had Other Plans.",
  "script": "I was shopping for paint in the same green jacket the store's employees wear when a woman marched over, demanding I find her a specific shade of touch-up paint. I told her twice that I didn't work there. She talked over me and said she would report me to my manager. A real employee walked over to help, but she claimed I had been rude and tried to get him in trouble too. He asked the front desk to check the camera near the paint aisle. The footage showed me calmly explaining myself twice while she ignored me. Store security walked her out for harassing staff, and the employee thanked me for staying calm. I still don't own a single can of that paint; unpaid customer service came with the jacket.",
